{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013a9tERxp2s8nXh5hwvBxwT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Criteria for Determining Irresponsible Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer-policies/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and related policies:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Policies\n\nReviewers who fail to submit reviews by the official deadline without submitting a personal emergency declaration will be automatically flagged as \"Highly Irresponsible.\"\n\nReviews that only contain a single argument (1-2 sentences) with no constructive feedback should be flagged when the submissions are good-faith work that merits a serious review. Additionally, extremely unprofessional reviews in tone (e.g., rude, racist, sexist, ableist content) may be penalized even if otherwise detailed.\n\n## Defining Good-Faith Submissions\n\nA good faith article at minimum states the contribution up front and provides an evaluation that supports it; if the writing is so poor that the intended contribution can't be identified or the evaluation is missing, it doesn't warrant a serious review. Papers with unclear stated contributions or insufficient evaluation do warrant serious reviews, and papers showing naivete about the state of the art still warrant serious reviews, but papers with complete lack of awareness of work in the field don't count as good faith submissions.\n\n## Author Reviewing Requirements\n\nThe policy covers non-submission of reviews on time without warning, extremely terse reviews for good-faith submissions, and egregious cases of unprofessional tone and LLM policy violations.\n\nThe search results did not contain specific details about the complete review form scoring criteria scale for EMNLP 2025. For detailed information about the specific scoring scale and review form structure, you may want to consult the official EMNLP 2025 website or the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31c0fb95-847c-42b3-bd47-a5416d2ede91","uuid":"f5e65567-9469-4f52-8418-b111d5707d70","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:13:48.554Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01M9RSkwA4gndhgvMWpox5HX","content":[{"title":"Criteria for Determining Irresponsible Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer-policies/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and related policies:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Policies\n\nReviewers who fail to submit reviews by the official deadline without submitting a personal emergency declaration will be automatically flagged as \"Highly Irresponsible.\"\n\nReviews that only contain a single argument (1-2 sentences) with no constructive feedback should be flagged when the submissions are good-faith work that merits a serious review. Additionally, extremely unprofessional reviews in tone (e.g., rude, racist, sexist, ableist content) may be penalized even if otherwise detailed.\n\n## Defining Good-Faith Submissions\n\nA good faith article at minimum states the contribution up front and provides an evaluation that supports it; if the writing is so poor that the intended contribution can't be identified or the evaluation is missing, it doesn't warrant a serious review. Papers with unclear stated contributions or insufficient evaluation do warrant serious reviews, and papers showing naivete about the state of the art still warrant serious reviews, but papers with complete lack of awareness of work in the field don't count as good faith submissions.\n\n## Author Reviewing Requirements\n\nThe policy covers non-submission of reviews on time without warning, extremely terse reviews for good-faith submissions, and egregious cases of unprofessional tone and LLM policy violations.\n\nThe search results did not contain specific details about the complete review form scoring criteria scale for EMNLP 2025. For detailed information about the specific scoring scale and review form structure, you may want to consult the official EMNLP 2025 website or the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) documentation directly."],"durationSeconds":7.703509629000004}}
