{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1NdbhVhBrsaJN9c3mNGz5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form overall assessment score scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 July | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FJuly\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form and overall assessment scoring:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nWhile the search results confirm that reviewers provide these three scores, the specific details about the 1-5 scale itself were not fully detailed in the official documentation retrieved. However, based on community discussions about ACL 2025 reviews, the overall assessment scores appear to follow a scale where scores range from 1 to 5, with descriptors like \"Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" for the highest scores.\n\nFor more specific information about the exact scale definitions and anchors, you may want to visit the official review form page directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31c0fb95-847c-42b3-bd47-a5416d2ede91","uuid":"d21d3f60-9603-4b55-8cd4-21da42eb078a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:13:56.423Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form overall assessment score scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KPM3eCMRLC5tmvwp2qpeQo","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 July | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FJuly"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form and overall assessment scoring:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nWhile the search results confirm that reviewers provide these three scores, the specific details about the 1-5 scale itself were not fully detailed in the official documentation retrieved. However, based on community discussions about ACL 2025 reviews, the overall assessment scores appear to follow a scale where scores range from 1 to 5, with descriptors like \"Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" 