{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Exau3uwDJK6RTvMPuCTq1G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n2\t\n3\t\\usepackage[review]{acl}\n4\t\n5\t\\usepackage{times}\n6\t\\usepackage{latexsym}\n7\t\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n8\t\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n9\t\\usepackage{microtype}\n10\t\\usepackage{inconsolata}\n11\t\\usepackage{graphicx}\n12\t\\usepackage{booktabs}\n13\t\\usepackage{amsmath}\n14\t\\usepackage{amssymb}\n15\t\\usepackage{multirow}\n16\t\\usepackage{xcolor}\n17\t\\usepackage{subcaption}\n18\t\n19\t\\graphicspath{{figures/}}\n20\t\n21\t\\title{Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors:\\\\ Why Confidence Signals Cannot Scale Structured Information Extraction}\n22\t\n23\t\\author{Anonymous}\n24\t\n25\t\\begin{document}\n26\t\\maketitle\n27\t\n28\t\\input{sections/abstract}\n29\t\\input{sections/introduction}\n30\t\\input{sections/related_work}\n31\t\\input{sections/method}\n32\t\\input{sections/experiments}\n33\t\\input{sections/discussion}\n34\t\\input{sections/conclusion}\n35\t\n36\t\\section*{Limitations}\n37\t\\input{sections/limitations}\n38\t\n39\t\\section*{Ethics Statement}\n40\tAll experiments use publicly available benchmarks (SciERC, CoNLL-2003, WNUT-17) and open-weight models (Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B).\n41\tCoNLL-2003 is based on the Reuters news corpus; we use the publicly available version and comply with its academic license terms.\n42\tNo new human data was collected or annotated for this study.\n43\tOur findings on signal limitations could inform more reliable deployment of IE systems by guiding practitioners toward appropriate confidence signals for their use case.\n44\t\n45\t\\bibliography{references}\n46\t\n47\t\\appendix\n48\t\\input{sections/appendix}\n49\t\n50\t\\end{document}\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NH2gxqJvj9Pis35Mu3qGGz","session_id":"31c0fb95-847c-42b3-bd47-a5416d2ede91","uuid":"76a6eed9-9ded-4983-9d3a-3b5c7d285d0a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:16:07.118Z"}
